    "input": "search_document: Based on the handbook excerpts provided, here is the definitive answer to your questions regarding the fees and the payment hold:\n\n**1. Responsibility for Foreign Transaction Fees**\nThe foreign transaction fees are **not** added by Northwind Outdoor. The handbook explicitly states that if your bank or card issuer charges a foreign transaction fee, this cost is determined by your financial institution and is not included in the displayed price. Northwind Outdoor does not apply any additional markup for currency conversion [payments.3]. Therefore, the fees you are seeing are strictly from your bank.\n\n**2. Releasing the Authorization Hold Faster**\nThe handbook does not provide a mechanism for Northwind Outdoor to manually release an authorization hold before the standard timeframe. It states that authorization holds typically last for 3 to 5 business days [payments.2]. The actual capture of funds only occurs after items are shipped [payments.2]. If the order is canceled before shipment, the authorization is released automatically within 7 business days, though some banks may take up to 10 business days to remove the hold [payments.2]. There is no mention of an expedited release process for holds in the provided text.\n\n**3. Immediate Resolution Options**\n*   **Switching Payment Methods:** You can switch your payment method to another accepted form (Visa, Mastercard, American Express, PayPal, or Apple Pay) [payments.1]. However, if you change your payment method to a new credit card, that new card must be verified within 48 hours, or the order will be canceled [order_changes.6].\n*   **Failed Payment Retry:** Since your card was declined, the order is automatically canceled. You have 48 hours to retry the payment with a different method [payments.4]. If you do not complete the payment within this window, the reserved inventory is released [payments.4].\n*   **Limits:** Ensure your new payment method can handle the transaction. The maximum single purchase amount for credit cards is $5,000.00 [payments.1]. If your bike exceeds this, you must split the payment or use an alternative method [payments.1].\n\n**Important Note on Urgency and Escalation**\nThe handbook excerpts do not contain information regarding in-store immediate processing overrides, manual hold releases, or specific procedures for resolving declined payments in a physical store setting beyond the standard online payment rules cited above. The handbook notes that if a payment is declined, the order is canceled and you have 48 hours to retry [payments.4]. It does not state that a human agent can bypass the 3-5 day hold period or the bank's processing schedule.\n\nBecause the handbook does not cover in-store emergency overrides or manual hold releases, I cannot provide a solution to bypass the wait time based solely on the provided text. I recommend speaking directly with a store manager or human agent who may have access to systems not described in these general handbook excerpts.",
